wn-header-what-is-this\">What is this?</h3>\n<p>New analytics events and attributes for feature flag interactions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>We now emit events on FF client initialization and failure</li>\n<li>We persist anonymous ID from <code>vscode</code> for analytics even after authentication</li>\n<li><code>Authenticate</code> button presses now report if they happened in local or remote env:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bitbucket.org/%7B%7D/%7B7fe83719-6bb0-4ca8-8508-dacc45c4d2ce%7D/images/461711928-image.png\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"markdown-header-how-was-this-tested\">How was this tested</h3>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>npm run lint\nnpm run test\nnpm run compile\n# poked around with things\n</code></pre></div>\n\n<p>‌</p>"}, "queued": false}, {"comment_count": 3, "task_count": 0, "type": "pullrequest", "id": 1053, "title": "Added parallel child properties to pipeline schema", "description": "According to the Bitbucket pipeline configuration reference [https://support.atlassian.com/bitbucket-cloud/docs/parallel-step-options/#Parallel](https://support.atlassian.com/bitbucket-cloud/docs/parallel-step-options/#Parallel){: data-inline-card='' } there are two child properties/options on `parallel` property:\n\n* steps\n* fail-fast\n\nThese are now added to pipeline schema in addition to array of `step` properties.\n\nValidation tool [https://bitbucket-pipelines.atlassian.io/validator](https://bitbucket-pipelines.atlassian.io/validator) was used to test these cases:\n\n```\npipelines:\n  pull-requests:\n    '**':\n      - parallel:\n        fail-fast: true\n        steps:\n          - step:\n          ...\n```\n\n```\npipelines:\n  pull-requests:\n    '**':\n      - step:\n      ...\n```\n\n```\npipelines:\n  pull-requests:\n    '**':\n      - parallel:\n        - step:\n        ...\n```\n\n‌", "state": "DECLINED", "draft": false, "merge_commit": null, "close_source_branch": false, "closed_by": {"display_name": "Bryan Wieger", "links": {"self":